      "role": "user",
      "content": "true, but wouldn't a company that powerful have people on the inside who are more loyal to the brand than to some random researcher? it just feels like if you're looking for it, you're never gonna find it because they already control the narrative. like, if i started noticing my own patterns or seeing weirdly specific ads that matched my mood, i'd probably just think i was being paranoid. how would anyone even prove this is happening if the data is so well hidden?",
