    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This concept touches on the difficulty of proving algorithmic intrusion, as surveillance capitalism often operates in the background. Proving such subtle correlation requires highly specialized forensic data analysis to trace inputs (gait data) to outputs (ads or profiles), which is not accessible to the general public. The \"narrative control\" you mention is a real barrier, as companies can legally frame data usage under terms of service that users often agree to without full comprehension. Therefore, proving it often requires whistleblowers with deep inside knowledge rather than surface-level observation.",
      "source": "target",
